            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for to lessen, then the French for to make up for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: le CV",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le CV — \"the CV, the résumé\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "J'ai envoyé mon CV à dix entreprises. I sent my CV to ten companies."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said cé-vé: short for Latin curriculum vitae. Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "CV is short for curriculum vitae, Latin for \"a running of life\": curriculum \"a running, a course\", from currere \"to run\", and vīta \"life\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
